    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4474188/Central-College/Senior-Database-Manager-for-Advancement": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Senior Database Manager for Advancement In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Senior Database Manager for Advancement Central College Apply Senior Database Manager for Advancement PELLA, IA • Advancement Apply Job Type Full-time Description The senior advancement database manager is responsible for oversight of reporting and list management, development compliance and data maintenance activities of the advancement office database; and oversight and assistance with gift processing and acknowledgments. Responsible for ensuring accurate campaign, financial and systems reports and compliance with campus, audit and federal/state regulatory policies. Lead work of advancement services, proactively driving and also delivering on requests for accurate dashboards, reports, lists, reminders, and all other information and records to assure the fulfillment of responsibilities and compliance. Understand and track using IRS, CASE and Central guidelines regarding the acceptance of gifts. Prepare reports and information for vice president, team, SLT, board and internal and external entities as needed. Partner, analyze and collaborate in campaign reporting and related campaign activities. Team lead for internal software, systems and processes that supports the work of fundraising, communications and stewardship, becoming a CRM superuser and the ability to train others. Supervise the recording of all gifts and pledges to Central and the accompanying responsibilities of generation of reports, receipts, pledge reminders, gift schedules, transmittals and other gift-related data as requested and serving as a point of contact for various external vendors and platforms. Responsible for strong partnership with financial aid in connecting annual Journey scholarship and endowed scholarship donors and students, ensuring donor criteria is met and communication plan is executed. Work collaboratively with other advancement staff for segmenting appeals and messaging, program materials and donor communications including lists for invitations, donor awards and recognitions, and program materials. Advise and prepare donor recognition for donor walls, displays and digital or print display. Responsible for data integrity of advancement records in partnership with all college records, identifying, leading and contributing to data projects related to data integrity and/or clean up. Provide unprompted insight and analysis of data to assist in the development of best practices throughout the advancement office, the campaign and to continue to professionalize the organization and the work of the advancement team. Assist with signature campus events including Homecoming, scholarship dinner, giving days including HooRah day and graduation. Requirements Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent, with five years effective experience in data, reporting, analytics or fundraising preferred. Expertise with non-profit or higher education data, software and reporting technologies helpful but not required. Willingness to learn CRM Advance and be a power user of this tool for data integrity, lists and segmentation. Central College Brand Expectations : Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4462073/Central-College/Upward-Bound-Advisor": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Upward Bound Advisor In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Upward Bound Advisor Central College Apply Upward Bound Advisor PELLA, IA • Pre-College Programs Apply Job Type Full-time Description As a member of the UB I/UBII administrative team, the person in this position provides academic support and college access services to program participants in assigned high schools and performs assigned administrative functions related to the purpose and objectives of the program. This federally funded position reports to the associate director of UB in the Pre-College Programs Department. Assume responsibility for individual and group meetings, events, and field trips for students at assigned schools: Assist with UB program participant recruitment and selection Develop and deliver UB college access curriculum to participants at assigned schools Monitor and record participants’ progress toward project objectives Travel to Des Moines Public Schools to provide academic, personal, and group advising for participants 1-2 days a week during the academic year Serve as advocate for participant needs at the target school by promoting tutoring opportunities, registration in rigorous coursework, etc. Actively participate in summer and academic year program planning/implementation: Attend staff meetings; complete program assessments as requested Contribute to curriculum review and development Participate in team planning/implementation of academic year and summer programs, activities, field trips, group college visits, and workshops Provide leadership, supervision, and accountability during UB events and field trips to ensure student well-being and event success Teach UB skills classes during the six-week summer session and related academic year workshop sessions as specified by the UB associate director Fulfill additional administrative roles as identified and assigned by the UB associate director. Assigned roles may vary from year-to-year depending on the needs of the program and the strengths of individual team member Maintain open and positive communication with parents of participants in assigned schools: Assist with basic planning for and attend parent information sessions Make parent contacts to provide college access and financial aid information or to offer additional assistance as necessary or as requested by the project director, associate director, or participants/parents Participate in school conferences, open houses, and other school events Maintain open and positive communication with target school personnel to secure/ensure: Provision of timely information to target school personnel regarding program activities and needs Meeting times/spaces, access to students, compliance with target school policies and practices Mutual exchange of information regarding participants’ needs and progress Positive relationships with target school leadership and personnel Maintain accurate, timely paper and electronic records as required by the grant or as requested by the director or assistant director: Keep accurate records of student participation and progress Accurately enter related data into program database in a timely fashion Maintain accurate up-to-date records of personal time and effort Note:  This position requires occasional evening or weekend hours during the academic year and extended hours during the six-week summer component. General responsibilities Maintain confidentiality with respect to participants’ academic and personal information Demonstrate commitment to personal professional growth Consistently demonstrate a positive attitude Must be open and adaptable to change Must work cooperatively and respectfully with others Perform other duties as assigned Requirements Bachelor’s Degree Three years of experience in education, student development, counseling, or related field. Ability to effectively develop working teams. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Competence with professional use of digital/electronic communication and social media. Ability to work effectively with students from diverse backgrounds Iowa driver’s license - this position requires regular travel to assigned target schools. Central College Brand Expectations Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4461962/Central-College/Talent-Search-Advisor": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Talent Search Advisor In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Talent Search Advisor Central College Apply Talent Search Advisor PELLA, IA • Pre-College Programs Apply Job Type Full-time Description As a member of the TS administrative team, the TS advisor provides academic support and college access services to program participants in assigned schools. The advisor performs assigned administrative functions related to the purpose and objectives of the program. This federally funded position reports to the TS assistant director in the Pre-College Programs Department. Assume responsibility for individual and group meetings, events, and field trips for students at assigned schools: Assist with TS program participant recruitment and selection Review, adapt, and present TS college access curriculum to participants at assigned schools Monitor and record participant progress toward project objectives Travel to Des Moines Public Schools to provide academic, personal, and group advising for participants 1-2 days a week during the academic year Provide leadership, supervision, and accountability during TS events and field trips to ensure student well-being and event success Serve as advocate for participant needs at the target school by promoting tutoring opportunities, registration in rigorous coursework, etc. Actively participate in program planning and professional development within the pre-college programs department and as a member of the TS team: Attend staff meetings, workshops, and professional development activities Support planning and implementation of field trips and events Maintain open and positive communication with parents of participants in assigned schools: Assist with basic planning for and attend parent information sessions for participants Make parent contacts to provide college access and financial aid information or to offer additional assistance as necessary or as requested by the project director or assistant director Participate in school conferences, open houses, and other school events Maintain open and positive communication with target school personnel to secure/ensure: Space and times for meetings, access to students, compliance with target school policies and practices Mutual exchange of Information regarding participants’ progress Maintain accurate, timely paper and electronic records as required by the grant or as requested by the director or assistant director: Keep accurate records of student participation and progress Accurately enter related data into program database in a timely fashion Maintain accurate up-to-date records of personal time and effort Note: This position may require occasional evening and weekend hours. General responsibilities Maintain confidentiality with respect to participants’ academic and personal information. Demonstrate commitment to personal professional growth. Consistently demonstrate a positive attitude. Must be open and adaptable to change. Must work cooperatively and respectfully with others. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree One to two years of experience in education, student development, counseling, or related field Must possess excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Driver’s license required - this position requires regular travel to assigned target schools Preferred Qualifications : Two years or more of experience in education, student development, counseling, or related field. Knowledge/experience with student financial aid, FAFSA, scholarship applications and/or college admissions Experience organizing/managing events and field trips involving large groups Central College Brand Expectations Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4349725/Central-College/Counselor-Part-Time": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Counselor (Part-Time) In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Counselor (Part-Time) Central College Apply Counselor (Part-Time) PELLA, IA • Student Development Apply Job Type Part-time Description The Part-Time Staff Counselor provides short-term mental health counseling, crisis assessment, referrals, consultation, and clinical documentation for Central College students. Working under the direction of the Lead Counselor, this position helps ensure students have timely access to quality mental health services while maintaining accurate clinical records and collaborating with campus partners to support student well-being. Clinical Counseling · Provide short-term individual counseling for students experiencing personal, emotional, behavioral, or psychological concerns. · Conduct intake assessments and develop appropriate treatment plans. · Assess and respond to students experiencing mental health crises, consulting with the Lead Counselor as appropriate. · Make referrals to community providers or higher levels of care when clinically indicated. · Maintain professional and ethical standards consistent with applicable licensing requirements and the American Counseling Association. Clinical Documentation · Maintain timely, accurate, and confidential clinical records in accordance with professional standards and applicable state and federal regulations. · Complete required documentation, case notes, treatment plans, referrals, and other clinical records. Consultation & Collaboration · Consult with faculty, staff, and Student Development colleagues while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. · Collaborate regularly with the Lead Counselor regarding student care, crisis response, and referral planning. · Participate in Counseling Center meetings and case consultation. Other Responsibilities · Participate in required trainings and professional development. · Assist with Counseling Center operations as assigned. · Perform other duties as assigned. Central College Brand Expectations : · Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. · Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. · Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. · Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. · Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Requirements Required Qualifications · Master's degree in Counseling, Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Social Work, Psychology, or a closely related field. · Licensed or license-eligible in the State of Iowa. · Experience providing individual counseling. · Strong clinical assessment, documentation, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications · Experience counseling college-age students or young adults. · Experience with crisis intervention. · Experience using electronic health records. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4433720/Central-College/Grounds-Technician": {
      "title": "Central College - Grounds Technician",
      "description": "Central College - Grounds Technician In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Grounds Technician Central College Apply Grounds Technician PELLA, IA • Facilities Management Apply Job Type Full-time Description Responsible to the Grounds Manager for performing a variety of grounds and general maintenance tasks. · Responsible for mowing, trimming, weeding, seeding, landscaping, planting, watering, and snow removal. · Assist with fertilizer and pesticide application (if licensed and certified). · Operate grounds equipment i.e., tractors, mowers, spreaders, push mowers, snow blowers according to safety requirements and guidelines. · Assist with basic maintenance of grounds equipment and other general maintenance tasks.. · Complete deliveries, office and furniture moves and resident housing bed bunking based on needs and project assignments · Support event set-up/tear down on campus/athletic grounds and in campus facilities. · Maintain clean shops and mechanical rooms. · Assist facilities staff with projects and tasks as needed Requirements · High School Diploma/GED and must be able to do simple math functions. · 1 year of effective experience and valid driver’s license required. · Ability to use/climb a ladder safely and lift, push & pull up to 100 pounds. · Must be able to work flexible hours for snow removal duties or other special events as needed Central Brand Expectations: · Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment. · Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. · Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. · Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. · Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4430700/Central-College/Part-Time-Accounts-Payable-Coordinator": {
      "title": "Central College - Part-Time Accounts Payable Coordinator",
      "description": "Central College - Part-Time Accounts Payable Coordinator In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Part-Time Accounts Payable Coordinator Central College Apply Part-Time Accounts Payable Coordinator PELLA, IA • Business Office Apply Job Type Part-time Description Reporting to the CFO & Controller, the Accounts Payable Coordinator is responsible for managing and coordinating the processing of invoices and payments owed by the College to its vendors and suppliers. This role ensures that all payments are accurate, timely, and compliant with College policies, while maintaining organized financial records and supporting month-end close processes. This position requires attention to detail, higher level conceptual skills, relentless pursuit of knowledge and intellectual curiosity. The successful candidate must possess strong analytical, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Accounts Payable Oversee the end-to-end operations of the accounts payable process, including invoice processing, payment runs, and expense report management. Ensure all payments are processed accurately, in a timely manner, and in compliance with College policies and regulatory requirements. Review vendor statements to College records for accuracy. Assist in the development and enforcement of accounts payable policies and procedures. Vendor Management Resolve vendor issues, (escalating when needed), discrepancies, or disputes effectively and professionally. Ensure accurate vendor records, including banking information and tax documents (e.g., W-9s). Compliance & Internal Control Monitor internal controls to safeguard College assets and prevent fraud. Assist Business Office leaders to ensure compliance with tax regulations, including sales/use tax and 1099 reporting requirements. Collaborate with auditors to support audit requests and to ensure accuracy and compliance. Process Improvement and Technology Utilization Identify and implement opportunities for process automation and efficiency improvements within the AP workflow. Other Promote an environment of collaboration, transparency, approachability, and support. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, business management or related field. Prefer 2 - 4 years relevant experience. Experience with Colleague software preferred. Microsoft Office experience required. Central College Brand Expectations Demonstrate a network of caring relationships by showing respect for others, being dependable and promoting cooperation with others in the work environment Be your best self by being accountable for responsibilities, adapting well to change and maintaining the highest standards of business ethics. Perform job responsibilities on campus to support the residential college environment. Strive to perform as effectively as possible while maintaining a high level of quality and promoting personal growth and development. Respect and comply with college rules and policies, including participation in required training courses; report any suspected violations of the Title IX policy to the Title IX Coordinator. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4419172/Central-College/Part-time-Event-Services-Employee": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Part-time Event Services Employee In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Part-time Event Services Employee Central College Apply Part-time Event Services Employee PELLA, IA • Event Services Apply Job Type Part-time Description Responsible to the Director of Events Services and Catering Manager for various support duties. This position assists with events and meals on Central’s campus, as well as other local venues. Hours vary according to Events, Catering needs, but will be primarily weekends with occasional weeknight hours . General Responsibilities · Assist with opening, food prep, station setup, closing tasks, and overall cleanup · Maintain a clean, organized, and sanitary work area and equipment · Present a clean, neat, and professional appearance at all times · Be open, adaptable, and flexible in a dynamic work environment · Work cooperatively and respectfully with team members, supervisors, and guests · Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors or management 14 - 15 Year Olds : · Help with setting up catering events. Maintaining buffet lines and perform server duties at various events. Ensuring dishes and pans are properly cleaned and stored. 16 – 17 years old - duties of 14-15 year old description plus: Help with prepping and setting up catering events. Maintaining buffet lines and perform server duties at various events. Ensuring dishes and pans are properly cleaned and stored. 18 years old and up · Duties of 14-17 year old descriptions plus bartending and ability to drive campus vehicles (after required certification). Requirements Must be at least 14 years old to apply 14-15 years old: May work no more than 3 hours a day on school days and no more than 8 hours a day on non-school days between hours of 7am and 7pm. May work no more than 18 hours a week when school is in session. Between June 1 and Labor Day, the evening end time is extended to 9pm. May work no more than 40 hours per week when school is not in session. Must have weekend availability Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/recruiting/jobs/Details/4419152/Central-College/Part-time-Dining-Services-Employee": {
      "title": "In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript.",
      "description": "Central College - Part-time Dining Services Employee In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Part-time Dining Services Employee Central College Apply Part-time Dining Services Employee PELLA, IA • Dining Services Apply Job Type Part-time Description Responsible to the Central Market Manager for various support duties. This position assists with events and meals in the Central Market. Hours vary according to Central Market needs, but will be primarily weekends with occasional weeknight hours . General Responsibilities · Assist with opening, food prep, station setup, closing tasks, and overall cleanup · Maintain a clean, organized, and sanitary work area and equipment · Present a clean, neat, and professional appearance at all times · Be open, adaptable, and flexible in a dynamic work environment · Work cooperatively and respectfully with team members, supervisors, and guests · Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors or management 14 - 15 Year Olds : · Duties may include ensuring dishes and pans are properly cleaned and stored, serving on main buffet line or salad bar, and with general cleaning duties in the dining area. 16 years old and older - duties of 14-15 year old description plus: · Maintain stations that may include buffet lines, salad bar, filling beverages, dishroom, and washing pots and pans. Prepare food, occasional knife usage, and operate equipment to fry, bake, and assemble a variety of food. Requirements Must be at least 14 years old to apply 14-15 years old: May work no more than 3 hours a day on school days and no more than 8 hours a day on non-school days between hours of 7am and 7pm. May work no more than 18 hours a week when school is in session. Between June 1 and Labor Day, the evening end time is extended to 9pm. May work no more than 40 hours per week when school is not in session. Must have weekend availability Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Central College: Privacy Policy"
