    "https://central.edu/job-seekers/benefits/": {
      "title": "Job Seekers",
      "description": "Benefits | Job Seekers | Central College Skip to main content Central College logo Admission Apply to Central Visit Campus Deposit Now Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition Price Admission Requirements Contact Us Dates and Deadlines Fast Facts International Students Outcomes Request Info Admission Ambassadors Student Profiles Transfer Students Academics Majors Academic Calendar Academic Programs Career Development Academic Success Deans Commencement Community Service Core Requirements Course Catalog & Schedule of Courses Faculty Fine Arts Geisler Library Honors (Emerging Scholars) Off-Campus Experiences Pre-Health Registrar’s Office Transcripts Campus Life Campus Dining Campus Map BELONG at Central Faith Fine Arts Frequent Questions Get Involved Health & Safety Life in Pella Living on Campus Move-In Guide Parent Info Student Handbook Student Senate Student Services Traditions Contact Us Alumni Stay Connected Initiatives Events Update Us Endowment Planned Giving Central Red Handshake Journey Scholarship Fund Ways to Give Dutchology Be The Good – Dutch Letter Homecoming Commencement Transcripts Imagine More A World of Good Athletics Sports Recruit Me Central Dutch Network Calendar Athletic Training Beyond Central Camps & Clinics Central Close-Up Central Club Facilities Hall of Honor Staff Directory Strength & Conditioning Spirit Shoppe Under Armour About Directory Events News Dutchology Apply Visit Tour Give About Directory Events News Dutchology Apply Visit Tour Give Central College logo Admission Apply to Central Visit Campus Deposit Now Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition Price Admission Requirements Contact Us Dates and Deadlines Fast Facts International Students Outcomes Request Info Admission Ambassadors Student Profiles Transfer Students Academics Majors Academic Calendar Academic Programs Career Development Academic Success Deans Commencement Community Service Core Requirements Course Catalog & Schedule of Courses Faculty Fine Arts Geisler Library Honors (Emerging Scholars) Off-Campus Experiences Pre-Health Registrar’s Office Transcripts Campus Life Campus Dining Campus Map BELONG at Central Faith Fine Arts Frequent Questions Get Involved Health & Safety Life in Pella Living on Campus Move-In Guide Parent Info Student Handbook Student Senate Student Services Traditions Contact Us Alumni Stay Connected Initiatives Events Update Us Endowment Planned Giving Central Red Handshake Journey Scholarship Fund Ways to Give Dutchology Be The Good – Dutch Letter Homecoming Commencement Transcripts Imagine More A World of Good Athletics Sports Recruit Me Central Dutch Network Calendar Athletic Training Beyond Central Camps & Clinics Central Close-Up Central Club Facilities Hall of Honor Staff Directory Strength & Conditioning Spirit Shoppe Under Armour Helpful Links: Academic Calendar Course Catalog Deposit Dutchology Majors & Programs myCentral Registrar Tuition About Directory Events News Apply Visit Tour Give Job Seekers home / Job Seekers / Benefits Benefits Employee Benefits at Central College At Central College, we are committed to supporting our employees’ health, well-being, and professional growth. Our comprehensive benefits package is designed to offer valuable resources and peace of mind, starting from your first day of employment. Health Insurance Eligible employees are offered health insurance beginning the first of the month following their hire or appointment date. Central College currently provides two options: a traditional HMO plan with access to a wide network of providers, and a high-deductible health plan (HDHP) that allows employees to contribute to a health savings account (HSA). The college shares the cost of health insurance premiums, with the employee’s portion deducted on a pre-tax basis for added tax savings. Dental & Vision Insurance Employees may also elect voluntary dental and vision coverage, effective the first of the month following hire. Coverage is available for individuals or families and is paid by the employee through pre-tax payroll deductions. Life Insurance Central College provides life insurance coverage equal to two times the employee’s annual salary, up to a maximum of $100,000. Supplemental life insurance is available for employees and their dependents at the employee’s expense. Retirement Plan Central College will contribute 2% of the employees’ annual salary after one year of employment. This amount will increase by 1% each year in July to a maximum of 6%. A mandatory employee contribution of 3% will begin after one year of employment. In addition, all employees may choose to contribute to a voluntary 403(b) retirement plan at any time. Tuition Benefits Full-time employees receive a 100% tuition reduction for Central College coursework, while employees working less than full-time receive a prorated benefit. Employees are eligible upon hire, with supervisor approval. After two years of continuous employment, spouses and dependents may receive a tuition reduction toward one degree program. Central also participates in two national tuition exchange programs—Tuition Exchange, Inc., and the Council for Independent Colleges (CIC), which may provide scholarship opportunities for dependent children of full-time employees. Please note that availability through these exchange programs may be limited based on institutional capacity and consortium requirements. Visit www.tuitionexchange.org or www.cic.edu for participating schools. Work and Life Balance Vacation: Vacation hours are awarded at the beginning of each fiscal year and are based on years of service. Relevant prior experience may be taken into consideration. Time is prorated for employees working less than full-time and for new hires. Unused vacation does not carry over into the following year. Sick/Medical: Eligible employees receive 80 hours of sick leave annually, prorated for those working less than full-time. Sick leave may be used for illness, injury, or medical appointments. Unused hours do not carry over into the next fiscal year. Parental Leave: Central provides five days of paid parental leave within the first 30 days following the birth of a child for the birthing parent and/or their spouse. Holidays: Central College offers a generous holiday schedule, which includes New Year’s Day, Good Friday, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Veterans Day (if honorably discharged), Thanksgiving Day, the day after Thanksgiving, Christmas Eve Day, and Christmas Day, as well as a campus closure between Christmas and New Year’s Day. Community Volunteer Time: Eligible employees receive 16 hours of paid time per fiscal year to participate in community service or volunteer opportunities. This benefit is prorated for employees working less than full-time. Employee ID & Campus Perks Your Central College ID is your pass to campus life! Free access to college events (where student fees don’t apply) Use of the library and fitness centers Discounts at the dining center, Spirit Shoppe, and local businesses Being part of Central means being part of a community, on campus and off. Questions? If you have any questions or would like more information about our employee benefits, please contact the Human Resources Office at 641-628-5156. We look forward to supporting you throughout your career at Central College. Job Seekers Benefits Information about Central Returning Applicants Policies Our Ethos Our Purpose Lead. Move. Inspire. From first-year jitters to student body president, kinesiology major Jay Kimbrough ’27 is already living out his future — inspiring young people to move, thrive and find joy in caring for themselves. Read More Request Information We're excited you're interested in Central! Submit your request and we’ll make sure you don’t miss any information about campus visit events, scholarship opportunities and more. Request Info Loading... This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply. Footer Quicklinks Academic Calendar Bookstore Brand Guidelines Campus Map Catering Services Central Dutch Network Commencement Conferences & Events Dutchology Employment Events Calendar Library Media Contacts Mission myCentral News Policies Pre-College Programs Safety Spirit Shoppe Title IX Central College Site 877-462-3687 641-416-4414 812 University St. Pella, Iowa 50219 admission@central.edu © Central College 2026 Privacy Policy"
    },
